      "annotation" : {
        "createdBy" : [ "Carrine Blank" ],
        "definition" : [ "Papaic digest of mammalian liver." ],
        "definition source" : [ "http://www.oxoid.com/uk/blue/prod_detail/prod_detail.asp?pr=LP0027&c=uk&lang=EN\n\nLIVER DIGEST NEUTRALISED\n\nCode: LP0027\n\nA biologically standardised papaic digest of liver for use as a source of nutrients in microbiological culture media.\n\nThe digest is water soluble and compatible with other culture media ingredients and may be sterilised by filtration or autoclaving; thus it is suitable for use as an integral part of many culture media or as a valuable supplement. Being derived from liver this product contains relatively high levels of iron. The profile shows the characteristic even spread of peptides obtained from papaic digests." ]
      },
